// Hub connection attempts the pipeline, the front door or the hub refused, per minute and instance.
// Backs the "hub connections are being refused" alert: a refusal is a negotiate or connect by a
// caller with no session or an expired one (401), from another origin (403), who is no member of
// the tenant, was deactivated there, reached a suspended tenant, or carried no hub claims. A few
// are normal as sessions and memberships change; a sustained rate is a stale SPA build retrying a
// tenant or a session it lost, or someone probing tenants. More than 30 a minute on one instance
// for five minutes is a starting point.
customMetrics
| where name == "tellma.realtime.connects"
| extend outcome = tostring(customDimensions["outcome"])
| where outcome == "refused"
| summarize refused = sum(valueSum) by cloud_RoleInstance, bin(timestamp, 1m)
| summarize minutes = countif(refused > 30) by cloud_RoleInstance, bin(timestamp, 5m)
| where minutes >= 5
